    "brand.tagline": "Green Footprint Int'l Co., Ltd. was founded in 2021 as a social enterprise established by the Taiwan Toy Library Association, building on the association’s more than 20 years of experience in toy recy",
    "brand.summary": "Green Footprint Int'l Co., Ltd. was founded in 2021 as a social enterprise established by the Taiwan Toy Library Association, building on the association’s more than 20 years of experience in toy recycling and parent-child education.\n\nWe have observed that up to 90% of children’s toys in Taiwan are made of plastic, yet their average lifespan is only around six months. According to estimates, from birth to the age of 12, each child may accumulate up to one tonne of plastic toys. Throughout their life cycle, these toys generate approximately 5.44 to 6.64 kilograms of CO₂-equivalent emissions per kilogram — equivalent to the weight of an adult elephant. This figure does not yet include the carbon footprint generated by transportation and marketing.\n\nTo extend the lifespan of toys and support a low-carbon transition, we established Toy Box in Taoyuan in 2023 — Taiwan’s first specialised second-hand toy store. Through this initiative, we aim to help children understand the value of resource conservation and environmental sustainability from an early age.\n\nSince 2024, Green Footprint has officially entered a new stage in the circular economy. We have begun dismantling and sorting discarded toys, transforming them into recycled plastic pellets and 3D printing filaments. By doing so, we aim to reduce reliance on petrochemical-based raw materials from the source and actively lower the carbon footprint of commercial activities.\n\nLooking ahead, we will design and manufacture a series of sustainable products that are 100% recyclable, including remade toys, educational tools, furniture, building materials, and artworks. We will also work with businesses, government agencies, and schools to promote ESG sustainability initiatives, while expanding opportunities for cross-sector collaboration and educational co-creation.\n\nWe believe that only by moving the concept of “recycling” from the end of the process to the very beginning — and by redefining every stage of design, production, and logistics — can we truly realise resource circularity and create a more sustainable path for the next generation.",
    "brand.product1.name": "re-ing Sustainable Balance Board",
    "brand.product1.desc": "The re-ing Sustainable Balance Board is a balance toy inspired by the shape of a potato chip, merging environmental responsibility with aesthetic design. Made from over 50% recycled plastic sourced from the Taiwan Toy Library, the product is crafted entirely from HDPE to ensure 100% recyclability. Utilizing mass-production techniques from the furniture industry, it breathes new life into post-consumer plastic and exemplifies circular economy in action. The design addresses the challenge of integrating recycled materials into the toy industry. Through balance-based play, the board encourages children to develop an early understanding of sustainable resource values. Its height and curvature are precisely calculated for stability and safety, making it suitable for users of all ages. It functions both as a balance board and as a seating cushion, with a hollow structure that reduces weight while increasing usability. The board's rounded form and vibrant marbled colors—created naturally by variations in the recycled material—make it not only a functional toy, but also a playful design accent for the home. Made from durable, waterproof, and UV-resistant materials, it is ideal for use in a variety of settings including balconies, gardens, and living rooms. Compared to traditional plastic toys, the re-ing Sustainable Balance Board combines material innovation, family interaction, and design-led education. It offers a hands-on, accessible way to experience circular design, setting a new standard for the sustainable toy industry by making environmental awareness tangible, fun, and integrated into everyday life."
